WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.434
-Tariq, we have a lot to get to.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:05.033
The book is available finally.
Right now. You can get it.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:08.033
Go to any bookstore,
local bookstore.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.367
You can go
to Barnes &amp; Nobles.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:11.367
Whatever you got to do.
-Wherever books are sold.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:14.567
-Wherever books are sold, you
can get "The Upcycled Self."

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:16.200
Congratulations, by the way,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.200
on your 11th Grammy nomination,
as well.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.534
-Thank you.
-I mean, this is...

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:22.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.200
You got nominated for your song
"Love Letters,"

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.133
which is a tribute to hip-hop.
-To hip-hop, yeah.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.868
A love letter to hip-hop

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:32.234
in celebration of,
you know, its 50th anniversary,

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.868
as well as
my 50th anniversary here.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.167
-Yeah. That's true.
That's right. Happy birthday.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.234
Happy...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.767
-Thank you.
-The -- A lot of it's

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:45.100
in the book of how you got
started in hip-hop and rap.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.434
Was it your cousin? Shawn?

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:48.167
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, Shawn and I.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:51.133
Well, you know Shawn,
who's now the Roots' manager.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:55.033
You know, my long-time,
you know, competitor.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:56.534
Yeah. We started --
-Was he?

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.033
-Yeah, he's about
two years older than me.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.300
And when we were young,
we would always compete

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.734
just with the --

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:04.434
first with, you know, sketching
and, like, visual art,

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:06.467
and then it sort of,
you know, elevated

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:10.133
into writing songs out of
our encyclopedias and stuff.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.634
We used the encyclopedia,
dictionaries and stuff

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:13.834
and write rhymes.

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:15.701
So, you know, he got nice.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.667
I think I started at around 9,

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.400
and by the time I was 11
and he was 13 or so,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.968
he made a record.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.901
He had, like, a piece of vinyl
that was pressed up,

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.734
and, you know,
so then that became

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:28.133
my life's mission, was,
you know, just getting better

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.000
than he was on that record.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.701
-What was -- Do you remember
one of your first rhymes?

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:35.033
-Of course. Well,
I've done my first rhyme.

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:38.200
I did it here, you know,
as a guest on the couch before.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.100
It's -- It was written that,
you know --

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.734
You know the style
of J.J. Fad, "Supersonic"?

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:44.834
Where it's like,
you know, just...

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.934
Summa-lumma-lumma-lumma-lumma...

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:50.133
Yeah, yeah, yeah. So I did --
I'd written one of those.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.000
And, yeah,
the rest is sort of history.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.234
-Yeah.

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:54.767
And before you were the Roots,

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.634
you were the Square Roots,
right?

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.200
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.734
-Who came up with that name?

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.234
-I think I came up
with the Square Roots.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.334
I think I thought of the logo
first, like, you know,

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:06.234
this is what could represent
the Square Roots.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.200
And it was sort of like,
you know, the square root,

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.067
that little check thing,
and I had the root underneath

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.200
the, you know --
under the umbrella.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.767
-Yeah. Yeah.
And that didn't stick?

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.434
-No, it didn't stick.
It didn't stick.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:18.534
But, I mean, you know,
it stuck long enough for us

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:21.300
to get our first merch
pressed up.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.501
You know, I think we did a gig
for someone,

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:24.601
and they paid us in T-shirts.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:28.467
They paid us
in Square Roots T-shirts.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:29.901
-I'll take it, man.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.667
-Did you have any other names
for the band

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.300
besides Square Roots?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.234
You know, we were Radioactivity
at one point.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.934
I think, you know,
we also entertained the idea

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:41.234
of calling ourselves,
like, Soul Fish or something.

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:42.567
I don't know. But it didn't --

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:44.434
-Soul Fish?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:46.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.667
-Soul Fish?

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.067
-It was what --

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.667
-Imagine if you were called
Soul Fish.

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.033
-Yeah.
-Yeah, I don't think --

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:54.734
I don't think that band
would have meant,

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:57.434
you know, what the Roots mean
to the culture.

00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:59.667
-No. Not Soul Fish.
-Right.

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.968
-Was Black Thought
always your name?

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:03.901
-Nah. Come on.
And you know it wasn't.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:05.567
You know Black Thought
wasn't always my name.

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:08.234
[ Drum roll ]
What was my name, Jimmy?

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:11.834
-Oh, my God. It's so good.
There's two of them.

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:15.000
There's one that's okay,
and there's one that's awful.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:20.701
One was called, like,
T Metaphor or something.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.701
-Yeah. Yeah. T Metaphor.
-T Adjective.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:23.968
-[ Laughs ] T Adjective.

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:26.801
-Yeah. Any Mad Lib.
T Metaphor.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.133
-Yes. Yeah. Yeah. T Metaphor.

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:29.868
That was one of them.
That was one.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.534
-Yeah. T Meta?
-Yeah.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:34.200
-Yeah, and then you had
something called, like --

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.033
I want to say Hawk Smooth?

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:38.934
-It was Hawk Smooth.
Yeah. It was an acronym.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:40.467
[ Laughter ]
It was an acronym.

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:42.300
-It was an acronym?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.934
It stood for -- It was
the Hype African Warrior

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:47.167
Kickin' it Smooth.

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.734
[ Applause ]

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:53.434
-Like --
-Good God!

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:54.968
-You know.
-Wow!

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.734
That's a long walk on that one.
Oh, my --

00:03:57.734 --> 00:04:00.667
Dude, imagine if you were
Hawk Smooth from Soul Fish.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:05.367
Hawk Smooth from Soul Fish
sounds like some dude --

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:07.968
Like, he works security at,

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.033
like, one of those
outdoor festivals

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.267
hoping to get recognized
when he's like,

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:13.868
"Right this way.
Gotta have your pass."

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.300
You go,
"Yo, is that Hawk Smooth?

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.567
-"Is that Hawk Smooth
from Soul Fish?"

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:19.968
-"No pictures, man.
Come on, man."

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.968
-Yeah, man.
-I love the book.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.434
I love the stories.
-Thank you.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:28.033
-I didn't know this much about
you there. It's a great story.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:32.000
And it's funny obviously because
you have a great sense of humor,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.868
but it's a lot of stuff, man.

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:36.300
You really worked your way
to get to where you are.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.667
-Yeah, yeah, for sure, for sure.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:40.033
-What does
"The Upcycled Self" mean?

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:43.601
-I think "The Upcycled Self"
is about just arriving

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.901
at a better version of oneself

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:47.467
and, like,
whatever that journey,

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:50.067
you know, sort of includes.

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:53.234
For me, you know, it's been
a personal trajectory

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:55.133
and it's been about addressing

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.400
and unpacking a lot
of the trauma of the past,

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.234
you know, and stuff
that, you know,

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:02.033
even my closest friends
didn't know about me

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:04.133
because I don't wear it
on my sleeve.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:06.200
But, yeah, I think
at this stage of the game

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.667
at this point in my career

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.634
and, you know, at this point
in the Roots' career,

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:12.133
I think we --
the idea is to be of service.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:13.501
Right? You know?

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:16.334
So I feel like, you know,
addressing this sort of thing

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:19.934
and, you know, just speaking
to my history in this way

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:22.300
is what's better --
what's going to best serve

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.834
my long-time fans
and supporters, you know?

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.567
Yeah, I would meet people
who, you know,

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:28.200
said some of the same thing,
in that,

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.067
"Yo, I've rocked with you
for such a long time.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:32.067
Long-time fan.
I felt like I knew you.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:34.300
I know your music.
But, you know, I didn't."

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.667
-And I like the idea
of upcycling.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.667
-Yeah, yeah.
-It's not recycling. but it's...

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:41.067
-Upcycling. Yeah. You don't
have to abandon everything.

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:44.100
You know, there's a quote from
Bruce Lee that says, you know,

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:47.200
"Adapt that which is useful,
abandon that which is not,

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.133
and add that which is uniquely
and specifically your own."

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:52.701
And I feel like
that's the upcycle, you know?

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:54.834
-Yeah. Yeah. I love it.

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.033
I think it's gonna inspire
a lot of people.

00:05:57.033 --> 00:05:59.400
I have to ask --
because I've been asking

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.834
for the last five, seven years.

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:04.501
When are we getting
a new Roots album?

00:06:04.501 --> 00:06:05.934
-Ooh. Uh...

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:08.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:09.701
Look --

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:10.834
-Questlove's peeking
over the cameras.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.167
-Right. Right.
I can say, you know,

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:15.400
the new Roots album is coming,
you know, hopefully soon.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:16.734
But I mean, you know,
let's just put --

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:18.167
let's put folks on the spot.

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:19.634
Ahmir, when's the new
Roots album coming?

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:21.300
-Hey, man!
-Right.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:25.400
-It's done when it's perfect.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.100
-Wow.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.400
-Well, this is perfect.
Congratulations. This is done.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:30.968
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:32.834
-"The Upcycled Self"
is available now.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:35.934
Tariq Trotter, everybody!
Go pick it up.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:38.467
More "Tonight Show" after the
break. Stick around, everybody.

